---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBox from '../components/CtaBox.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Nearshore Customer Service in Mexico & Colombia — Teleforce',
  serviceType: 'Bilingual nearshore customer service outsourcing (Mexico, Colombia)',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Teleforce' },
  areaServed: ['US', 'CA'],
  description:
    'Bilingual nearshore customer service from Mexico and Colombia — native English/Spanish talent, full U.S. time-zone overlap, and lower cost than U.S. in-house.',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Nearshore Customer Service in Mexico & Colombia | Teleforce"
  description="Nearshore customer service in Mexico & Colombia — bilingual, Hispanic-market talent at U.S.-hours overlap and less than half the in-house cost. Request a proposal."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <header class="ahead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cat">Nearshore talent</div>
      <h1>Nearshore Customer Service in Mexico &amp; Colombia</h1>
      <div class="ameta"><span>Native EN / ES</span><span>U.S.-hours overlap</span><span>30-year operator</span></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap" style="margin-top:24px">
    <img class="feature-img" src="/brand/image1.jpg" alt="Nearshore bilingual customer service team in Mexico and Colombia" loading="lazy" />
  </div>

  <article class="post">
    <p class="lead"><strong>Nearshore customer service</strong> in Mexico and Colombia gives U.S. companies bilingual, Hispanic-market support talent that works your business hours — at less than half the cost of hiring in-house. It's the sweet spot between expensive domestic teams and far-offshore vendors that trade cost for a time-zone gap and an accent your customers notice.</p>

    <h2>Two of the strongest nearshore talent pools</h2>
    <p>Latin America is one of the few regions where native-level Spanish and strong English coexist at scale, on U.S. business hours. Mexico and Colombia are its two deepest customer-service talent pools:</p>
    <h3>Mexico</h3>
    <p>A large native bilingual workforce, especially in northern metros, plus the tightest cultural alignment with U.S. Hispanic customers and near-total time-zone overlap. Ideal when your Spanish-speaking base skews Mexican-American and same-day, in-person proximity matters.</p>
    <h3>Colombia</h3>
    <p>One of South America's deepest bilingual BPO talent pools, with strong, intentionally-developed English proficiency and a mature contact-center sector in Bogotá and Medellín. Ideal for bilingual depth at volume.</p>

    <h2>Bilingual, Hispanic-market support built in</h2>
    <p>A large share of U.S. customers prefer Spanish — and English-only support quietly costs you retention with that segment. Nearshore agents from Mexico and Colombia serve English and Spanish from the same seat, natively, so no customer hits a two-tier experience. For the full argument, see <a href="/blog/bilingual-customer-support-us-companies">why bilingual customer support is no longer optional</a>.</p>

    <h2>The cost advantage</h2>
    <p>Compare loaded cost to loaded cost. Once you add benefits, management, tools, recruiting, attrition, and idle capacity to a U.S. in-house hire, a nearshore seat in Mexico or Colombia typically lands at <strong>less than half the total cost</strong> — without the quality and time-zone tradeoffs of far-offshore.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Mexico / Colombia (nearshore)</th><th>Far offshore</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Spanish</td><td>Native</td><td>Rare / accented</td></tr>
        <tr><td>English</td><td>Strong, neutral</td><td>Variable</td></tr>
        <tr><td>U.S. time-zone overlap</td><td>Full</td><td>10–12 hr gap</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cultural affinity (U.S. Hispanic)</td><td>High</td><td>Low</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fully-loaded cost vs. U.S.</td><td>Less than half</td><td>Lowest, but with tradeoffs</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <CtaBox
      heading="Scope a nearshore team for your book"
      body="Tell us your volumes and languages. We'll come back with a staffing plan and a go-live date — usually within two business days."
      label="Request a proposal"
    />

    <h2>Deeper dives</h2>
    <ul class="svc-list" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
      <li><a href="/blog/mexico-customer-support-outsourcing">Mexico customer support outsourcing</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/colombia-call-center-outsourcing">Colombia call center outsourcing</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/nearshore-customer-support-latin-america">Comparing LatAm support hubs</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/spanish-customer-service-outsourcing">Spanish customer service outsourcing</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Running a SaaS product? This talent powers our <a href="/outsourced-saas-support">outsourced SaaS support</a> teams.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <h3>Is nearshore customer service in Mexico or Colombia better?</h3>
    <p>Both are excellent; the right pick depends on your mix. Mexico offers the tightest cultural alignment with Mexican-American customers and near-total time-zone overlap; Colombia offers exceptional bilingual depth at volume. Many programs blend both.</p>
    <h3>Do the agents work U.S. hours?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Both countries sit within U.S. business-hours overlap, so support and escalations happen in real time — not on an overnight lag.</p>
    <h3>How much can we save vs. hiring in the U.S.?</h3>
    <p>Typically more than half, on a fully-loaded basis, once benefits, management, tools, recruiting, and attrition are counted. Teleforce prices per engagement — request a proposal for your numbers.</p>
  </article>

  <section class="contact" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--amber)">Request a proposal</div>
      <h2 class="disp" style="color:#fff">Build a nearshore team in Mexico or Colombia.</h2>
      <p class="sub" style="color:var(--on-dark-mut);max-width:60ch">Tell us your volumes and languages. A human comes back with a staffing plan and a go-live date — usually within two business days.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:22px"><a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-amber">Request a proposal</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
